
==============================================================================
DIAGNOSING THE SWEEP
==============================================================================

-- The best corner of the sweep box
   utility 200.860 | 47 repeaters | 18/18 pairs served
   So the ceiling seen in the sweep is a property of the sample,
   not of the hardware. Saltelli and Latin hypercube samples put
   very few points near a corner of a four-dimensional box, and
   the two-dimensional grids hold the other two parameters at
   their midpoints by construction.

-- How good does each parameter have to be, with the others at their best
   Generation rate (Hz)       needs at least 7.448e+04
   Coherence time T2 (s)      needs at least 0.01661
   Link fidelity F_L          needs at least 0.9742
   Swap success q_s           needs at least 0.8966
   wrote results\w2_requirements.csv  (4 rows)

   Read this as a hardware requirement: with everything else at the
   top of its published range, this is the level each parameter has
   to reach before the nine city network can serve all of its
   traffic.

-- How far outside the rate approximation is this network
   worst-link success probability on the chosen paths:
     median 0.00237, worst 9.12e-06
   memories per node needed for W * p_min = 1:
     median 422, worst 109,648
   memories per node actually modelled: 100

   across the sweep: 5286 of 5286 solves have W * p_min < 1
     median 0.0332, worst 7.87e-05

-- What that means, stated plainly
   Eq. (2) of the paper is R = q_s^(h-1) W p_min, and the paper says
   it holds where W p_min >> 1. On this network it never does.

   The reason is the O band. At 0.35 dB/km an 80 km link transmits
   1.58e-03 of the photons sent, so reaching W p_min = 1
   needs about 631 memories per node. The paper's own
   experiments use 100. At the C band value of 0.2 dB/km the same
   link transmits 2.51e-02, needing about 40, which is
   why the approximation is reasonable in their setting and not in
   ours.

   This is a finding, not a bug. Moving a placement model from the
   C band to the O band breaks an approximation the published model
   relies on, and the fix is either far more multiplexing or a rate
   equation that stays valid at low p. It belongs in the report as
   a limitation and in the next stage as a question.

==============================================================================
DIAGNOSIS COMPLETE
==============================================================================
